+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deploy review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+Not "ship it with caveats". The contract as committed **cannot take a single deposit
+against the real USDT at `0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`** — `deposit()`
+reverts unconditionally on mainnet (A-01). And if that one line were fixed, the vault
+would then pay depositors **0% yield** while permanently burying every dollar of Aave
+interest it earns in an address no function can reach (A-03).
+
+Nothing under `src/` was modified. Every failure below is the contract exactly as it
+sits in commit `7186d60`.
+
+---
+
+## Contents
+
+| ID | Severity | Finding |
+|---|---|---|
+| [A-01](#a-01) | **Critical** | `deposit()` reverts against real USDT — the vault is inoperable on mainnet |
+| [A-03](#a-03) | **Critical** | Aave interest is never credited to shares and is permanently unrecoverable |
+| [A-04](#a-04) | **High** | The withdrawal fee accrues to nobody — it is stranded, contradicting the README |
+| [A-05](#a-05) | **High** | Uncapped, un-timelocked `setDepositFee` lets the owner take a depositor's entire deposit |
+| [A-06](#a-06) | **High** | `pause()` freezes withdrawals; `renounceOwnership()` makes the freeze permanent |
+| [A-02](#a-02) | Medium | Real USDT rejects a non-zero→non-zero `approve` (matters for the A-01 fix) |
+| [A-07](#a-07) | Medium | No received-amount measurement; deposits break if Tether re-enables its transfer fee |
+| — | Info | [What held up under attack](#what-held-up) · [Why the green tick lied](#why-the-green-tick-lied) |
+
