+<a name="a-01"></a>
+## A-01 — Critical — `deposit()` reverts against real USDT. The vault cannot be used.
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:94`
+
+```solidity
+usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+`usdt` is typed `IERC20`, whose `approve` is declared `returns (bool)`. Solidity emits
+an ABI-decode of 32 bytes of return data after the call. The real TetherToken's
+`approve` is declared `public` with **no return value** and returns zero bytes. The
+decode reverts, so `deposit()` reverts — always, for every caller, for every amount.
+
+`safeTransferFrom` on line 93 is fine because `SafeERC20` tolerates empty returndata.
+Line 94 is the only unguarded call and it is enough to brick the contract.
+
+The existing suite cannot see this: `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` is a stock OpenZeppelin
+`ERC20`, and OZ's `approve` returns `true`.
+
+**Evidence — against the real token on a mainnet fork:**
+
+```
