+<a name="a-04"></a>
+## A-04 — High — The withdrawal fee accrues to nobody. The README says otherwise.
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:16-18` and `README.md` both state:
+
+> Both fees stay supplied in Aave and accrue to the remaining shareholders rather than
+> being swept to the owner.
+
+That is true of the deposit fee (line 97 adds the gross `amount` to
+`totalAssetsStored` while line 90 mints shares on the net, which does lift the share
+price). It is **false** of the withdrawal fee. Line 117 subtracts the **gross** amount
+from `totalAssetsStored` while line 119 only pulls the **net** out of Aave:
+
+```solidity
+totalAssetsStored -= grossAssets;          // line 117
+aavePool.withdraw(address(usdt), netAssets, msg.sender);   // line 119
+```
+
+So the fee leaves the accounting *and* stays in Aave. It raises nobody's share price.
+It joins the A-03 pile of unreachable aUSDT.
+
+**Evidence:**
+
