+<a name="a-05"></a>
+## A-05 — High — The owner can take a depositor's entire deposit by raising the fee.
+
+`setDepositFee` has no upper bound, no timelock, and no delay:
+
+```solidity
+function setDepositFee(uint256 newFeeBps) external onlyOwner {
+    depositFeeBps = newFeeBps;
+    ...
+}
+```
+
+Because the deposit fee is implemented as *"mint shares on the net, but credit the
+gross to the pot"*, a high fee is not a fee at all — it is a direct transfer of the
+depositor's money to whoever already holds shares. At 9,999 bps, 99.99% of an incoming
+deposit is handed to the incumbents.
+
+An owner who holds even a token position can front-run a pending deposit in the
+mempool with a single `setDepositFee` call and take essentially all of it. No
+compromise of any other component is required; the owner key alone is enough.
+
