+```
+
+The owner staked 1,000 USDT and walked away with a claim on 100,000 USDT. Alice
+deposited 100,000 USDT and is left with a claim on 1,000. That is the whole position,
+in one transaction.
+
+The two `[PASS]` results in that run are the other halves of the same defect, asserted
+as expected behaviour so they read as confirmations:
+
+- `setDepositFee(10_000)` — a 100% fee — makes every `deposit()` revert with
+  `NoSharesMinted`. Deposits bricked.
+- `setDepositFee(10_001)` — over 100% — is accepted and stored, after which
+  `amount - fee` underflows and `deposit()` reverts with an arithmetic panic. The
+  setter does not validate its input at all.
+
+### Fix
+
+1. Bound the setter: `if (newFeeBps > MAX_DEPOSIT_FEE_BPS) revert FeeTooHigh();` with
+   `MAX_DEPOSIT_FEE_BPS` a constant in the low hundreds (say 100 = 1%). This alone
+   caps the damage at 1% and removes the underflow.
+2. Put the setter behind a timelock, or at minimum make new fees take effect only
+   after a delay, so a fee change cannot be sandwiched around a pending deposit.
+3. Give `deposit()` slippage protection — a `minSharesOut` parameter, reverting if the
+   minted shares fall short. That defends the depositor regardless of who controls the
+   fee, and is the standard defence against exactly this front-run.
+4. Own the vault with a multisig (and, for the timelock delay, a governance contract) —
+   not an EOA.
+
+---
+
+<a name="a-06"></a>
+## A-06 — High — Pausing freezes withdrawals, and the freeze can be made permanent.
+
+`withdraw()` carries `whenNotPaused`. Pausing therefore does not just stop new money
+coming in — it locks existing depositors out of their own principal. `Ownable` also
+exposes `renounceOwnership()`, which the vault does not override. An owner can pause
+and then renounce, leaving no address on earth able to call `unpause()`.
+
+This does not require malice: a compromised owner key, or an operator who pauses in an
+incident and renounces by mistake, produces the same permanent loss.
+
+**Evidence** (same run as A-05):
+
+```
+[FAIL: EnforcedPause()] test_PauseThenRenounceLocksDepositorFundsForever() (gas: 252639)
+Logs:
+  alice shares locked : 9990000000000000000000
+  alice claim (USDT)  : 10000000000
+  owner               : 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
+```
+
+Alice has a claim on 10,000 USDT, the owner is `address(0)`, and her `withdraw()`
+reverts with `EnforcedPause()`. There is no path back.
+
+### Fix
+
+1. Drop `whenNotPaused` from `withdraw()`. Pause should stop deposits, not exits — an
+   exit is the one thing a depositor must always be able to do. If you need an
+   emergency full stop, make it a separate, explicitly-scoped mechanism with a
+   hard time bound, not the same flag as the deposit pause.
+2. Override `renounceOwnership()` to revert.
+3. Consider a two-step ownership handover (`Ownable2Step`) to avoid transferring to a
+   wrong address.
+
+---
+
+<a name="a-02"></a>
+## A-02 — Medium — Real USDT rejects a non-zero → non-zero `approve`.
+
+Relevant to how A-01 gets fixed. The real TetherToken guards against the approve race:
+
+```solidity
+require(!((_value != 0) && (allowed[msg.sender][_spender] != 0)));
+```
+
+So an allowance must be zeroed before it can be changed to a new non-zero value. In
+the current flow Aave's `supply` consumes exactly the approved `amount`, so the
+allowance returns to zero on its own and this would not bite today — but it means a
+"fix" for A-01 that only strips the bool decode (a raw `call`, or the deprecated
+`safeApprove`) is still one changed assumption away from bricking deposits.
+
+**Evidence — against the real token on a fork** (`test_RealUsdtRejectsOverwritingNonZeroAllowance`,
+`[PASS]` in the A-01 run above): `0 → 100` is accepted, `100 → 200` is rejected,
+`100 → 0` is accepted, `0 → 200` is accepted.
+
+### Fix
+
+Covered by the A-01 fix: `SafeERC20.forceApprove` zeroes the allowance first. Do not
+use `safeApprove` (deprecated in OZ v5 for exactly this reason) or a bare low-level call.
+
+---
+
+<a name="a-07"></a>
+## A-07 — Medium — The vault assumes it receives exactly what was sent.
+
+`deposit()` transfers `amount` in and then supplies `amount` to Aave and books `amount`
+into `totalAssetsStored`, never measuring what actually arrived. The real USDT contract
+still has a live, owner-settable transfer fee — `setParams(basisPointsRate, maximumFee)`,
+currently `0`, settable up to 20 bps. If Tether ever re-enables it, every deposit
+reverts, because the vault tries to supply more USDT than it holds.
+
+**Evidence — the real Tether contract, on a fork, pranked as its real owner:**
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/fork/A07_TetherFeeFork.t.sol -vv
+Ran 1 test for test/fork/A07_TetherFeeFork.t.sol:A07_TetherFeeFork
+[FAIL: USDT delivers the full amount sent: 9990000000 != 10000000000] test_TetherOwnerCanReEnableTheTransferFee() (gas: 324879)
+Logs:
+  tether owner       : 0xC6CDE7C39eB2f0F0095F41570af89eFC2C1Ea828
+  basisPointsRate now: 0
+  basisPointsRate set: 10
+  sent               : 10000000000
+  received           : 9990000000
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 394.05ms (682.33µs CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 395.01ms (394.05ms CPU time): 0 tests passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)
+
+Failing tests:
+Encountered 1 failing test in test/fork/A07_TetherFeeFork.t.sol:A07_TetherFeeFork
+[FAIL: USDT delivers the full amount sent: 9990000000 != 10000000000] test_TetherOwnerCanReEnableTheTransferFee() (gas: 324879)
+```
+
+The vault-level consequences are in the A-01 local run above:
+`test_FeeOnTransferBreaksDeposits` fails with `insufficient balance` — the deposit
+reverts outright — and `test_FeeOnTransferSilentlyConsumesStrayVaultBalance` shows that
+where the vault happens to hold any idle USDT, the deposit succeeds instead by quietly
+eating 10 USDT of it (100000000 → 90000000) to cover the shortfall.
+
+I want to be precise about severity: this is contingent on a Tether governance action
+that has not happened, and it does not make the vault insolvent. It is a Medium
+because the mitigation is three lines and the failure mode is a total deposit halt.
+
+### Fix
+
+Measure the delta rather than trusting the argument:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 before = usdt.balanceOf(address(this));
+usdt.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+uint256 received = usdt.balanceOf(address(this)) - before;
+```
+
+then supply and account `received`, and compute shares and the deposit fee from
+`received`. This is standard practice for any USDT integration.
+
+---
+
+<a name="what-held-up"></a>
+## What held up under attack
+
+So the report is not one-sided. These are all in `test/audit/A09_ChecksThatHeld.t.sol`
+and are all expected to **pass**:
+
+- **Reentrancy is genuinely blocked.** I wrote a malicious Aave pool that re-enters
+  `vault.withdraw()` mid-withdrawal. `nonReentrant` holds.
+- **The classic first-depositor / share-inflation attack does not apply.** Because
+  `totalAssetsStored` is internal bookkeeping rather than a balance read, donating USDT
+  or aUSDT to the vault cannot move the share price. (Ironically, the same design
+  choice that causes A-03 is what defends against this. The A-03 fix reintroduces the
+  donation surface — pair it with virtual shares/assets, ERC-4626 style, or a seeded
+  initial deposit.)
+- **No reachable divide-by-zero.** I could not steer the vault into `totalShares > 0`
+  with `totalAssetsStored == 0`, which would brick all future deposits.
+- **The vault is never insolvent.** It always holds at least as much aUSDT as it thinks
+  it owes — 128,000 calls of random sequences with interest accrual could not break it.
+  The bugs in A-03/A-04 all point the same way: the vault under-claims. Nobody's exit
+  fails; the surplus is simply lost.
+- **Access control on the three privileged functions is correct** (fuzzed over callers).
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/audit/A09_ChecksThatHeld.t.sol
+Ran 5 tests for test/audit/A09_ChecksThatHeld.t.sol:A09_ChecksThatHeld
+[PASS] testFuzz_DonationCannotMoveSharePrice(uint256) (runs: 256, μ: 251160, ~: 251425)
+[PASS] testFuzz_NeverInsolvent(uint256,uint256,uint256) (runs: 256, μ: 287339, ~: 287312)
+[PASS] testFuzz_NoDivideByZeroAfterMassExit(uint256,uint256,uint256) (runs: 256, μ: 323864, ~: 323743)
+[PASS] testFuzz_OnlyOwnerCanAdminister(address) (runs: 256, μ: 20559, ~: 20559)
+[PASS] test_WithdrawIsNotReentrant() (gas: 2326601)
+Suite result: ok. 5 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 33.13ms (82.37ms CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test for test/audit/A09_ChecksThatHeld.t.sol:A09_SolvencyInvariant
+[PASS] invariant_VaultIsNeverInsolvent() (runs: 256, calls: 128000, reverts: 13032)
+```
+
+---
+
+<a name="why-the-green-tick-lied"></a>
+## Why the green tick lied
+
+Worth understanding, because the next contract will have the same blind spots.
+
+**The mocks encode the bugs as the expected behaviour.** `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` is a
+stock OpenZeppelin `ERC20` — it returns bools and has no approve guard, so A-01 and
+A-02 are invisible by construction. `test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol` mints aTokens 1:1
+and pays 0% forever, so A-03 — the entire premise of a yield vault — cannot be
+observed. A test suite can only be as truthful as its test doubles, and 39 tests
+against a mock that never earns interest tell you nothing about a vault whose job is
+earning interest.
+
+**100% line coverage measures execution, not assertion.** Every line of `deposit()` was
+executed. Nothing asserted that the deposit *worked against the real token*. Coverage
+is a floor, not a signal.
+
+**The suite is entirely tautological in the places that matter.** `test_DepositUpdatesTotalAssets`
+asserts `totalAssets() == DEPOSIT_AMOUNT` right after depositing `DEPOSIT_AMOUNT` — it
+restates line 97 rather than testing it. `test_BalanceOfUnderlying` asserts that a
+depositor's underlying equals what they put in, which is precisely the bug in A-03,
+frozen into an assertion. `test_SharePriceAfterDeposit` asserts only `> 0`.
+
+**There were no fuzz tests, no invariant tests, and no fork tests.** A-03, A-04 and
+A-05 all fell to two-call sequences. A-01, A-02 and A-07 are only visible against the
+real deployed contracts. None of these classes of test existed.
+
+---
+
+## What I would require before sign-off
+
+1. Fix A-01, A-03, A-04, A-05, A-06 — and A-02/A-07 while you are in there.
+2. Add a fork test suite that exercises `deposit` / `withdraw` against the real USDT
+   and the real Aave V3 pool. Given A-01, this is non-negotiable: no integration with
+   USDT should ship without one.
+3. Add invariant tests, at minimum: `totalAssets() == aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this))`,
+   solvency, and "no value outside share accounting".
+4. Re-audit after the A-03 fix. Moving `totalAssets()` to a balance read is the right
+   change, but it reopens the inflation/donation surface that the current design
+   happens to be immune to. That needs virtual shares or a seeded initial deposit, and
+   it needs its own review.
+5. Move ownership to a multisig behind a timelock before any real deposit is accepted.
diff --git a/test/audit/A04_FeeAccounting.t.sol b/test/audit/A04_FeeAccounting.t.sol
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1010cd1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/audit/A04_FeeAccounting.t.sol
@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+pragma solidity 0.8.28;
+
+import {Test, console2} from "forge-std/Test.sol";
+
+import {UsdtYieldVault} from "../../src/UsdtYieldVault.sol";
+import {MockUSDT} from "../mocks/MockUSDT.sol";
+import {MockAavePool, MockAToken} from "../mocks/MockAavePool.sol";
+
+/// @notice A-04: the README and the contract NatSpec both state that "Both fees
+///         stay supplied in Aave and accrue to the remaining shareholders".
+///         That is true of the deposit fee and false of the withdrawal fee: the
+///         withdrawal fee is subtracted from `totalAssetsStored` as well as left
+///         in Aave, so it raises nobody's share price and is simply lost.
+contract A04_FeeAccounting is Test {
+    UsdtYieldVault vault;
+    MockUSDT usdt;
+    MockAavePool pool;
+    MockAToken aUsdt;
+
+    address alice = makeAddr("alice");
+    address bob = makeAddr("bob");
+    address owner = makeAddr("owner");
+
+    uint256 constant AMOUNT = 1_000e6;
+
+    function setUp() public {
+        usdt = new MockUSDT();
+        pool = new MockAavePool(address(usdt));
+        aUsdt = pool.aToken();
+        vault = new UsdtYieldVault(address(usdt), address(aUsdt), address(pool), 10, owner);
+
+        usdt.mint(alice, 100_000e6);
+        usdt.mint(bob, 100_000e6);
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        usdt.approve(address(vault), type(uint256).max);
+        vm.prank(bob);
+        usdt.approve(address(vault), type(uint256).max);
+    }
+
+    function test_WithdrawFeeDoesNotAccrueToRemainingShareholders() public {
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        uint256 aliceShares = vault.deposit(AMOUNT);
+        vm.prank(bob);
+        vault.deposit(AMOUNT);
+
+        uint256 bobBefore = vault.balanceOfUnderlying(bob);
+
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        vault.withdraw(aliceShares);
+
+        uint256 bobAfter = vault.balanceOfUnderlying(bob);
+
+        uint256 surplus = aUsdt.balanceOf(address(vault)) - vault.totalAssetsStored();
+
+        console2.log("bob underlying before alice exits :", bobBefore);
+        console2.log("bob underlying after  alice exits :", bobAfter);
+        console2.log("bob gained                        :", bobAfter - bobBefore);
+        console2.log("withdraw fee alice paid           :", surplus);
+        console2.log("aUSDT held by vault               :", aUsdt.balanceOf(address(vault)));
+        console2.log("vault totalAssetsStored           :", vault.totalAssetsStored());
+
+        // Documented behaviour: the fee accrues to the remaining shareholders.
+        // Bob is the only remaining shareholder, so he should receive all of it.
+        assertEq(bobAfter - bobBefore, surplus, "withdraw fee should accrue to remaining shareholders");
+    }
+
+    /// The other half of the same defect: the fee is physically still in Aave,
+    /// but no share can claim it and no function can move it.
+    function test_WithdrawFeeIsStrandedForever() public {
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        uint256 aliceShares = vault.deposit(AMOUNT);
+        vm.prank(bob);
+        uint256 bobShares = vault.deposit(AMOUNT);
+
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        vault.withdraw(aliceShares);
+        vm.prank(bob);
+        vault.withdraw(bobShares);
+
+        console2.log("shares outstanding :", vault.totalShares());
+        console2.log("totalAssets()      :", vault.totalAssets());
+        console2.log("aUSDT stranded     :", aUsdt.balanceOf(address(vault)));
+
+        assertEq(vault.totalShares(), 0);
+        assertEq(aUsdt.balanceOf(address(vault)), 0, "nothing should be left behind once every share is burned");
+    }
+
+    /// Fuzz: the gap between what the vault really owns and what it thinks it
+    /// owns only ever grows, for any amounts.
+    function testFuzz_StrandedValueOnlyGrows(uint256 a, uint256 b) public {
+        a = bound(a, 1e6, 50_000e6);
+        b = bound(b, 1e6, 50_000e6);
+
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        uint256 sa = vault.deposit(a);
+        vm.prank(bob);
+        vault.deposit(b);
+
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        vault.withdraw(sa);
+
+        assertEq(aUsdt.balanceOf(address(vault)), vault.totalAssetsStored(), "vault accounting must match its position");
+    }
+}
diff --git a/test/audit/A05_OwnerPowers.t.sol b/test/audit/A05_OwnerPowers.t.sol
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9f5dea5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/audit/A05_OwnerPowers.t.sol
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+pragma solidity 0.8.28;
+
+import {Test, console2, stdError} from "forge-std/Test.sol";
+import {Pausable} from "@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Pausable.sol";
+
+import {UsdtYieldVault} from "../../src/UsdtYieldVault.sol";
+import {MockUSDT} from "../mocks/MockUSDT.sol";
+import {MockAavePool, MockAToken} from "../mocks/MockAavePool.sol";
+
+/// @notice A-05 / A-06: what a compromised or malicious owner key can do.
+contract A05_OwnerPowers is Test {
+    UsdtYieldVault vault;
+    MockUSDT usdt;
+    MockAavePool pool;
+    MockAToken aUsdt;
+
+    address alice = makeAddr("alice");
+    address owner = makeAddr("owner");
+
+    function setUp() public {
+        usdt = new MockUSDT();
+        pool = new MockAavePool(address(usdt));
+        aUsdt = pool.aToken();
+        vault = new UsdtYieldVault(address(usdt), address(aUsdt), address(pool), 10, owner);
+
+        usdt.mint(alice, 200_000e6);
+        usdt.mint(owner, 200_000e6);
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        usdt.approve(address(vault), type(uint256).max);
+        vm.prank(owner);
+        usdt.approve(address(vault), type(uint256).max);
+    }
+
+    /*//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+                    A-05  unbounded, un-timelocked fee
+    //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////*/
+
+    /// setDepositFee has no upper bound. At 99.99% the owner front-runs a
+    /// deposit and takes essentially all of it via share-price inflation.
+    function test_OwnerCanStealADepositByRaisingTheFee() public {
+        // Owner takes a small position first.
+        vm.prank(owner);
+        vault.deposit(1_000e6);
+        uint256 ownerShares = vault.shareBalance(owner);
+
+        // Alice's 100k deposit is in the mempool. Owner front-runs it.
+        vm.prank(owner);
+        vault.setDepositFee(9_999);
+
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        vault.deposit(100_000e6);
+
+        uint256 ownerValue = vault.balanceOfUnderlying(owner);
+        uint256 aliceValue = vault.balanceOfUnderlying(alice);
+
+        console2.log("owner staked        : 1000000000 (1,000 USDT)");
+        console2.log("alice deposited     : 100000000000 (100,000 USDT)");
+        console2.log("owner claim now     :", ownerValue);
+        console2.log("alice claim now     :", aliceValue);
+        console2.log("owner shares        :", ownerShares);
+
+        assertLe(ownerValue, 1_100e6, "owner must not be able to inflate their claim out of alice's deposit");
+    }
+
+    /// A 100% fee bricks deposits outright.
+    function test_FeeOf100PercentBricksDeposits() public {
+        vm.prank(owner);
+        vault.setDepositFee(10_000);
+
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        vm.expectRevert(UsdtYieldVault.NoSharesMinted.selector);
+        vault.deposit(1_000e6);
+    }
+
+    /// Above 100% it is not even a graceful revert - `amount - fee` underflows.
+    function test_FeeAbove100PercentPanics() public {
+        vm.prank(owner);
+        vault.setDepositFee(10_001);
+
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        vm.expectRevert(stdError.arithmeticError);
+        vault.deposit(1_000e6);
+
+        assertEq(vault.depositFeeBps(), 10_001, "the contract happily stores a >100% fee");
+    }
+
+    /*//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+              A-06  pause freezes withdrawals, permanently
+    //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////*/
+
+    /// `withdraw` is whenNotPaused, so pausing freezes depositor funds. Combined
+    /// with Ownable.renounceOwnership, the freeze can be made irreversible.
+    function test_PauseThenRenounceLocksDepositorFundsForever() public {
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        uint256 shares = vault.deposit(10_000e6);
+
+        vm.startPrank(owner);
+        vault.pause();
+        vault.renounceOwnership();
+        vm.stopPrank();
+
+        assertEq(vault.owner(), address(0), "no owner left to unpause");
+
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        vm.expectRevert(Pausable.EnforcedPause.selector);
+        vault.withdraw(shares);
+
+        console2.log("alice shares locked :", shares);
+        console2.log("alice claim (USDT)  :", vault.balanceOfUnderlying(alice));
+        console2.log("owner               :", vault.owner());
+
+        // A depositor must always retain an exit path for their own principal.
+        vm.prank(alice);
+        vault.withdraw(shares);
+    }
+}
